<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I401677b1f2c5919a75dd9765038619f86a6a49ad" commit="416da662b1a996daff46f2f654fbf02393cce0f4" commit_message="manifest: adopt branch chromeos-5.37 for chromiumos/third_party/bluez  Branch chromeos-5.37 is based on BlueZ 5.37 release with Chromium-specific patches on top. BlueZ will be updated to 5.37 version by switching the branch to chromeos-5.37.  BUG=chromium:573950 TEST=run bluetooth autotest suite against the following platform(passing rate): samus(22/22), daisy_skate(22/22), chell(8/22), nyan_kitty(0/2), peach_pi(22/22), veyron_minnie(22/22), ninja(2/22), falco(8/22) and cyan(8/22)  Change-Id: I401677b1f2c5919a75dd9765038619f86a6a49ad Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/331858 Commit-Ready: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Miao-chen Chou &lt;mcchou@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Ning Huang &lt;wnhuang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="331858" owner_email="mcchou@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/58/331858/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ifc0e58150ef02f94551212efe506292a3e2d87e2" commit="90a8655669e12ef4f56408065275d356bb494266" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: ASoC: nau8825: Use TESTDAC to reduce start/stop playback plop&quot;  This reverts commit 1e1adb85c37fe8c356b555e83c24bb39a850562c. The reverted commit is replaced by (&quot;ASoC: nau8825: fix issue that pop noise when start playback&quot;)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49737,chrome-os-partner:49738 TEST=Reduced playback start pop and no headphone playback noise on Chell  Change-Id: Ifc0e58150ef02f94551212efe506292a3e2d87e2 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332521 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332521" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/332521/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8e1c9071a6f8b64a6bdc92e4b4e0ca1055e492d6" commit="f7f071ce645f1033c8c76f68069cd478df056615" commit_message="Revert &quot;CHROMIUM: ASoC: nau8825: Unground HPL/HPR before playback&quot;  This reverts commit 0e033c29f4c3973743944fd725b3b1ce89372929. The reverted commit is replaced by (&quot;ASoC: nau8825: fix issue that pop noise when start playback&quot;)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49737,chrome-os-partner:49738 TEST=Reduced playback start pop and no headphone playback noise on Chell  Change-Id: I8e1c9071a6f8b64a6bdc92e4b4e0ca1055e492d6 Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332522 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332522" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/22/332522/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I7fb4952c6f772e61393551f9b735b260caa8f20a" commit="202c1a1bf8b3a2ad32a8b50369a723d74555cfbb" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: fix issue that pop noise when start playback  Reduce pop noise in power up and down sequence when playback. The DAPM widgets graph is reconstructed to ensure the register write sequence at playback matches exactly to the v5 clickless sequence provided by Nuvoton.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 45d5eb3a342f2ef3d6dae16b074fdd9a01992fb5) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49737,chrome-os-partner:49738 TEST=Reduced playback start pop and no headphone playback noise on Chell  Change-Id: I7fb4952c6f772e61393551f9b735b260caa8f20a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332208 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332208" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/08/332208/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4da1d7e517c2bf04418656f3a9de9f26ee6aab1e" commit="4518e3cd1f9894237252126b63ef64d67951f283" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ASoC: Intel: boards: Use FS as nau8825 sysclk in nau88125_ssm4567 machine  256FS sysclk gives the best audio quality per nau8825 datasheet.  Loud headphone pop happens if there is no sysclk during nau8825 playback power up sequence. Currently Skylake does not output MCLK/FS when the back-end DAI op hw_param is called, so we cannot switch to MCLK/FS in hw_param. This patch reduces pop by leting nau8825 keep using its internal VCO clock during widget power up sequence, until SNDRV_PCM_TRIGGER_START when MCLK/FS is available.  This is a temporary fix before Intel ADSP can output MCLK/FS early.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49737,chrome-os-partner:49738 TEST=Reduced playback start pop  Change-Id: I4da1d7e517c2bf04418656f3a9de9f26ee6aab1e Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332524 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332524" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel